# The elaborator's door (notes/elaborate.md "What it reads and writes"): `wap wap/extensions/theory/elaborate/door.wap
# --tree <root> program.wap` checks the prelude of the wap tree <root> (wap/extensions/theory/prelude/) and then reads a
# program as it is written, the arguments, levels and types it leaves out found, and takes its statements in order
# (file.wap). A program's declaration of a name the prelude declares hides the prelude's from there on. A declaration
# is elaborated, checked by the kernel and added, and nothing is said of it; `type of e` prints e's type, `axioms of
# name` the axioms it rests on. The first refusal is printed as its one line and ends the run with a failure.
use "file.wap"
use "read.wap"

door_elaborated(Theory(), args)
